From bef69ad9c8ae3590ab78919aff8766b105f024c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Allen <cma@bitemyapp.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:23:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Animate view changes made through animator

A view's animator is now a forwarding proxy instead of the view itself.
Each change made through it runs in an animation group, its own unless
one is open, with implicit animation allowed for that change alone, so a
layer-backed view's frame, bounds and alpha interpolate on the render
thread over the group's duration and timing function while ordinary
setters in the same group still apply at once. Completion handlers are
scheduled in the common run loop modes, so they run while a control
tracks the mouse or a modal loop is open, as the animation itself keeps
being displayed. A window's animator is still the window.

Signed-off-by: Chris Allen <cma@bitemyapp.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
